; Regression (2026-09-20): an unknown identifier in the RECEIVER position of a
; member access — the sibling of xfail_unknown_return, one level in. `t.field`
; where nothing in scope declares `t` was neither resolved nor reported, so the
; access was emitted against whatever the slot held: a `let`-bound result
; SIGSEGVs, an unbound call is DROPPED at rc 0. The recognition rule was that
; the code had NO EFFECT WHATSOEVER — a new condition that never fires — and it
; cost ../tscaly/packages/tscaly a whole elision branch that ran every gate green.
;
; ★The receiver reaches the planner as ONE DOTTED NAME, not as a base with a
; chain, and dotted names were exempt wholesale (the namespace machinery owns
; them). What is judged is the FIRST SEGMENT; `unknown_name_ok.scaly` is the
; control for every dotted form that must stay legal.
; xfail: error: unknown identifier: nosuchthing

define Box (v: int)

function reads_a_stranger(x: int) returns int
{
    if (nosuchthing.v & 1) <> 0
        return 111
    222
}

let n reads_a_stranger(0)
